.TH AUDITPROV 2
.SH NAME
auditprov \- agent-provenance emitter for the tamper-evident audit log
.SH SYNOPSIS
.EX
include "auditprov.m";
auditprov := load AuditProv AuditProv->PATH;

init:     fn(): string;
attach:   fn(addr: string): string;
dialraw:  fn(addr: string): (ref Sys->FD, string);
attachfd: fn(fd: ref Sys->FD): string;
attached: fn(): int;
put:      fn(data: array of byte): (string, string, string);
get:      fn(score: string): (array of byte, string);
sha256:   fn(data: array of byte): string;
log:      fn(source, event, msg: string, payload: array of byte): int;
.EE
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B Auditprov
extends the audit log served by
.IR auditfs (4)
with content-addressed payloads, so that bulky agent-provenance
content \(em prompts, tool arguments and results, completions \(em can
be sealed into the tamper-evident trail without bloating the chain.
The payload is stored in a
.IR ventisrv (8)
content store as a vac hash tree; the audit record carries three
fields appended to its message:
.EX
	content=<score> sha256=<hex> size=<n>
.EE
.I Score
is the venti score of a packed vac entry describing the payload
(fetch it with
.IR auditget (1)
or
.BR get ).
.I Sha256
is the SHA-256 digest of the raw payload.
The score is only a locator; the SHA-256 is the integrity pin, and it
is sealed under the SHA-256 hash chain of
.IR auditfs (4),
so venti's SHA-1 addressing cannot be used to equivocate a payload
after the fact.
.PP
.B Init
loads the underlying modules and must be called first.
.B Attach
dials the content store and performs the venti handshake;
an empty
.I addr
resolves via the
.B auditventi
environment variable, then the default
.BR tcp!127.0.0.1!17034 .
.B Dialraw
dials without handshaking, returning a connection descriptor that a
parent may hand to a namespace-restricted child (the descriptor
survives
.BR pctl(NEWNS) );
the child completes the handshake with
.BR attachfd .
.PP
.B Put
stores a payload and returns its score and SHA-256;
identical payloads dedupe to the same score.
.B Get
fetches a payload back by score.
.B Log
combines the two: it stores
.I payload
(when non-nil) and seals one record via
.IR audit (2)'s
append-only sink
.BR /mnt/audit/log .
It returns 0 on success and \-1 if the record could not be sealed.
If the payload cannot be stored, the record is still sealed with
.B content=unstored
(the event is never lost) and \-2 is returned; the caller decides
whether that is fatal (see
.B Audit->ONFILE
for the fail-closed convention).
.SH SOURCE
.B /appl/lib/auditprov.b
.SH SEE ALSO
.IR auditget (1),
.IR auditfs (4),
.IR ventisrv (8),
.IR venti (2)
.br
.B /doc/compliance/audit-log-design.md
